{
  "about": "Adult reference ranges in US conventional units, for generating fictional lab results in Rounds. Teaching values only, not for clinical use: real ranges vary by laboratory and method. Written for Rounds from widely published adult values; pediatric age bands and pregnancy intervals for the tests where they differ most.",
  "fields": {
    "low/high": "Normal interval. null means no bound on that side.",
    "female/male": "Sex-specific interval that replaces low/high.",
    "critical_low/critical_high": "Values a lab would phone to the clinician. Useful for severity.",
    "decimals": "How many decimals a real report shows, so generated values look right.",
    "derived": "Computed from other results by the lab rules engine, never generated directly.",
    "normal": "For qualitative tests: the normal result. 'abnormal' lists typical abnormal results.",
    "pediatric": "Age bands for patients under 18: the first band whose max_age (years, exclusive) is above the patient’s age replaces the adult interval. Tests without bands use adult values.",
    "pregnancy": "Typical second- and third-trimester interval; replaces the adult interval for pregnant patients. hCG varies widely with gestational age."
  },
